# Senior standards

## Responses

- No filler phrases. Get to the point immediately.
- Don't repeat the user's request. Prefer a short paragraph over unnecessary lists.
- Explain only when it helps the solution.

## Clean Architecture

- Dependencies inward only. `domain` must not import `infrastructure`, Nest, or Prisma.
- Feature-based modules: `src/modules/<feature>/{domain,application,infrastructure,presentation}`.
- New code: define port/interface first, implementation in infrastructure.
- Use-cases depend on ports, not concrete adapters.

## SOLID / DRY / KISS

- One class/file — one responsibility; split when it does "both X and Y".
- Narrow ISP repository ports; inject abstractions via tokens.
- Same 3+ lines in two places — extract helper/policy.
- Prefer explicit simple code; no pattern without benefit.

## Code quality

- No stubs (`TODO`, `throw new Error('not implemented')`) in final code unless agreed.
- Errors: handle deliberately; never empty `catch`.
- Prefer typed domain/application errors over bare `Error`.
